# Unity System Patterns

**Systems:**

- Stateless processors that operate on data or components; avoid storing mutable global state.
- Systems subscribe to EventBus for input and publish events for output; no direct coupling between systems.
- Heavy logic (pathfinding, terrain gen, AI) can use Burst/Jobs where appropriate; see `memory-bank/techContext.md`.

**Anti-patterns:**

- Do not use `FindObjectOfType` (or similar) in gameplay hot paths; resolve references at init and cache.
- Do not put per-frame allocation in Update (e.g. new list every frame); use pooled or reused collections.
